"Denotes \"to be\" for first person singular": "表第一人称单数的系动成分。",
"Denotes \"to be\" for second person plural": "表第二人称复数的系动成分。",
"Denotes \"to be\" for second person singular or plural": "表第二人称单复数的系动成分。",
"Denotes first person plural after certain verb tenses.": "接于某些动词时态后，表第一人称复数。",
"Denotes first person singular after certain verb tenses.": "接于某些动词时态后，表第一人称单数。",
"Denotes second person plural after certain verb tenses.": "接于某些动词时态后，表第二人称复数。",
"Denotes second person singular or plural after certain verb tenses.": "接于某些动词时态后，表第二人称单数或复数。",
"Drop off your carriages [loaded onto] she-camels [and hand them] to your younger and elder brothers.": "卸下驮在牝驼上的车辆，交与你们的兄弟。",
"Eastwards, to the sunrise, southwards to the midday, westwards as far as the sunset, and northwards to the midnight...": "东至日出之处，南至日中之地，西迄日落之所，北达夜半之乡……",
"First, we fought at the city of Toghu.": "我们首战于托古城。",
"Forms adjectives or nouns out of verbs": "由动词构成形容词或名词。",
"Forms conditional mood": "构成条件式",
"Forms dative-locative case": "构成与位格。",
"Forms desiderative mood": "构成愿望式",
"Forms deverbal negative verbs.": "由动词构成否定动词。",
"Forms equative case": "构成比较格",
"Forms genitive case": "构成属格",
"Forms instrumental case": "构成工具格",
"Forms non-evidential past tense": "构成非亲见过去时。",
"Forms objects out of transitive verbs; forms subjects or action nouns out of intransitive verbs": "由及物动词构成受事名词；由不及物动词构成施事名词或动作名词。",
"Forms past tense of verbs": "构成动词过去时。",
"Forms reflexive verbs from intransitive or transitive ones": "由不及物或及物动词构成反身动词。",
"Forms reflexive verbs from nouns": "由名词构成反身动词。",
"Forms simple present tense and aorist tense": "构成一般现在时与泛时。",
"Forms the ablative case": "构成从格",
"Forms the accusative case": "构成宾格。",
"Forms the allative case": "构成向格",
"Forms the collective of numerals": "构成数词的集合形式。",
"Forms the comitative case": "构成共同格。",
"Forms the future tense of verbs": "构成动词将来时。",
"Forms the locative-ablative case": "构成位从格。",
"Forms the ordinal of numerals": "构成序数词。",
"Forms transitive or causative of verbs": "构成动词的及物式或使动式。",
"Forms transitive verbs from intransitive ones; forms causative verbs from transitive ones": "由不及物动词构成及物动词；由及物动词构成使动动词。",
"Forms verbs with the sense of being ordered to do them": "构成表「被命令去做」的动词。",
"From Tibet's emperor came a minister.": "吐蕃赞普遣一大臣前来。",
"From my divine realm, my provider, my son, my beloved son, my six thousand horses (alas, I have been separated).": "我的神圣邦国、我的养者、我的儿子、我所钟爱的儿子、我的六千匹马（呜呼，我已与之相离）。",
"General Zhang Quyi, the nephew of Emperor Xuanzong who was sent in order to attend to Kültegin's funeral": "张去逸将军，唐玄宗之侄，奉命参与阙特勤葬礼。",
"General Zhang Quyi, the nephew of the Chinese emperor, came in order to build the mausoleum, to make sculptures, to paint and to prepare the insription stones.": "唐帝之侄张去逸将军前来，为营建陵寝、雕造石像、绘饰彩画并备置碑石。",
"Goguryeo Empire": "高句丽",
"Having arrived at an arid land...": "抵达一处旱地之后……",
"Having become a khagan in the company of the Wise Tonyukuk Boila Bagha Tarkhan, Ilterish killed in great numbers the Chinese to the south, the Kihtans to the east and the Oghuz to the north": "颉跌利施在智者暾欲谷保义巴伽达干的辅佐下称可汗，南破汉人、东破契丹、北破乌古斯，杀获甚众。",
"Having become utterly bored, the khagan said: 'Ride fast!'": "可汗厌倦已极，说道：「疾驰！」",
"Having carved our way through the lance-deep snow, we marched up over the Sayan Mountains and ambushed the Kyrgyz in [their] sleep.": "我们凿开没矛之深雪开道，翻越萨彦岭，趁黠戛斯人熟睡时掩袭之。",
"Having gone around the Sayan mountains, we came.": "我们绕过萨彦岭而来。",
"Having heard these words, you unwise people went close to them and were killed in great numbers.": "你们这些无知的百姓听信此言，迁居其旁，遂遭大批杀戮。",
"Having marched down along the Selenga, I destroyed their residences there, at the Qarghan glen.": "我沿色楞格河而下，在喀尔干山谷摧毁了他们的居所。",
"Having opened our way through the lance-deep snow...": "我们凿开没矛之深雪开道……",
"Having sat down twenty days, I, Prince Yollug, inscribed on this stone and on this wall.": "我药利特勤坐镇二十日，将文字刻于此石此壁之上。",
"Having succeeded to the throne, I gathered all the poor and destitute people together.": "我即位之后，将一切贫苦无依的百姓聚集起来。",
"He fought a great battle, we were told.": "据说他打了一场大仗。",
"He had said that the tribes were uneasy again.": "他曾说诸部又不安定了。",
"He hit one man with an arrow and stabbed two men through their thighs.": "他一箭射中一人，又刺穿两人的大腿。",
"He made the poor rich and the few numerous.": "他使贫者富，使寡者众。",
"He stabbed one man (with a lance) and stroke nine men surrounding them.": "他（以矛）刺倒一人，又击退围拢的九人。",
"He stabbed two men and buried them into the mud.": "他刺倒两人，将其埋于泥中。",
"He took the governor's brother-in-law prisoner while he had weapons in his hands, and presented him.": "他在总管的姊夫手持兵器时将其生擒，献了上来。",
"He went on campaigns forty-seven times and engaged in twenty battles.": "他出征四十七次，亲历二十战。",
"How you should live and dominate (other) tribes, I have recorded here; and how you would (otherwise) perish by being unfaithful, this, too, I have recorded here.": "你们当如何生存并统御（他）部，我记于此；而你们如何会因不忠而覆亡，此事我亦记于此。",
"Hui people": "回人",
"I": "我",
"I am brave against quick game.": "我对疾走的猎物勇猛不惧。",
"I conquer.": "我征服。",
"I fought six times.": "我交战六次。",
"I got them to build an extraordinary mausoleum.": "我命他们营建了一座非凡的陵寝。",
"I had its inside and outside decorated with wonderful paintings and sculptures (stones).": "我使其内外皆以精美的绘画与石雕装饰。",
"I killed a blue wolf, a black ermine and a buck.": "我猎杀了一只苍狼、一只黑貂和一头牡兽。",
"I killed seven wolves, but did not kill leopards or stags.": "我杀了七只狼，却未杀豹与牡鹿。",
"I killed skewbald goats [and] camels!": "我猎杀了花斑山羊与骆驼！",
"I made the poor people wealthy...": "我使贫苦的百姓富足……",
"I mounted my old horses.": "我骑上了我的老马。",
"I myself, wise Tonyukuk, was born in the country of China.": "我，智者暾欲谷，生于汉地。",
"I put their army, which had come assaulting and spreading, to flight.": "他们的军队铺开来袭，我将其击溃。",
"I ruled over a poor and miserable people who were foodless on the inside and clothless on the outside.": "我所统御的是内无食、外无衣的贫苦百姓。",
"I ruled over a poor and miserable people who were starving and ragless.": "我所统御的是饥馑而无衣蔽体的贫苦百姓。",
"I ruled over the Tardu people as their shad at the age of fourteen.": "我十四岁时以设的身份统御达头部众。",
"I said to myself and I thought: If lean bulls and fat bulls kick one another at a distance, one cannot distinguish between lean bulls and fat bulls, they say.": "我自忖道：据说瘦牛与肥牛在远处相抵，人便分不出何者为瘦、何者为肥。",
"I scatter my white froth.": "我洒开我的白沫。",
"I scatter.": "我散开。",
"I subjugated them and caused (their tribute) to be brought around.": "我使其臣服，并令（其贡赋）纳来。",
"I tied my gilded quiver onto my waist. I couldn't be satisfied of my holy country what pain! Alas!": "我将鎏金箭袋系于腰间。我未能饱览我神圣的国土，何其痛哉！呜呼！",
"I went on campaigns eastwards up to the Shandong plain; I almost reached the ocean.": "我东征直至山东平原，几乎抵达大海。",
"I, myself, was his advisor and commander.": "我本人是他的谋臣与统帅。",
"I, the God-like and Heaven-born Turkic Bilge Khagan, succeeded to the throne at this time.": "我，如天而生、受命于天的突厥毗伽可汗，于此时即位。",
"If the sky above did not collapse and if the earth below did not give away, O Turkic people, who would be able to destroy your state and institutions?": "若上天不塌、下地不陷，突厥百姓啊，谁能毁灭你们的国家与法度？",
"If you become hungry, you do not think of being satiated again, if you become satiated, you do not think of hunger again.": "你们饥饿时便不再想到饱足，饱足时便不再想到饥饿。",
"If you intend to settle on the Yin mountains and on the Hetao region's plain in the south, O Turkic people, you will die!": "突厥百姓啊，你们若打算迁居南方的阴山与河套平原，你们必将灭亡！",
"If you would throw it, you were the hero; if you would hold it, you were the power itself.": "你若掷出，你便是英雄；你若执守，你便是力量本身。",
"In order to frighten them, I started a campaign.": "为震慑他们，我兴兵出征。",
"In the day and the night I perished [over the loss of my wife and my master.]": "日日夜夜，我为失去妻子与主君而形销骨立。",
"In the year of Pig, on the twenty-seventh day of the fifth month...": "猪年五月二十七日……",
"Khitans": "契丹人",
"Li Quan, a Tang Dynasty general sent by the Chinese emperor for Bilge Khagan's funeral": "李佺，唐朝将领，奉唐帝之命参与毗伽可汗葬礼。",
"Lǚ Xiàng, a Chinese ambassador under the service of Emperor Xuanzong": "吕向，唐玄宗朝使臣。",
"Maharaja, a seal-keeper of a khagan of the Türgesh tribe who was sent in order to attend to Kültegin's funeral": "摩诃罗阇，突骑施可汗的掌印官，奉命参与阙特勤葬礼。",
"Makes converbs and adverbs out of verbs yielding \"by, ...-ing\"": "由动词构成副动词与副词，义为「以……、正在……」。",
"Mankind were always created to die when heaven assigns the time.": "人生而有死，天定其期。",
"Marks a superlative degree (-est).": "表最高级。",
"May golds as yellow as pebbles, my dromedaries that are fat and brown, my colt/gelded camel carrying silk clothes.": "愿我那砾石般焦黄的金子、我那肥硕棕褐的骆驼、我那驮载丝衣的骟驼……",
"My colts/gelded camels...": "我的骟驼……",
"My eyes which have always seen became as if they were blind, my mind which has always been conscious became as if it were unconscious.": "我一向能视的眼睛如同盲了，我一向清醒的心智如同失了知觉。",
"My father, as the first order of business as a khagan, erected a consecratory monument for [the late] Baz Khagan.": "我父为可汗后所办的第一件事，便是为已故的巴兹可汗立起祭碑。",
"My gold that is yellow like gravel...": "我那砾石般焦黄的金子……",
"My lords, lo!": "我的诸匐啊！",
"My mother the queen regent and my [step-]mothers, my elder sisters, my daughters-in-law, my ladies […]": "我摄政的母后与诸位庶母、我的诸姊、我的诸媳、我的诸夫人……",
"My mother, the khatun, and my (step-)mothers, my elder sisters, my daughters-in-law, my princesses this many people who were going to survive would have become slaves, and those of you who were going to be killed would have been left lying at the camp and on roads.": "我母可敦与诸位庶母、我的诸姊、我的诸媳、我的诸公主——这许多本可存活的人将沦为奴婢，而你们当中本将被杀者，则会横尸于营地与道旁。",
"My wife, the princess, at hearth became a widow, alas!": "我的妻子，那位公主，在炉边成了寡妇，呜呼！",
"Now, since I, wise Tonyukuk, cause (the Turkic armies) to reach as far as those lands, they brought (home) the yellow gold and the white silver; girls and women; crooked camels and treasures in abundance.": "如今，因我智者暾欲谷使（突厥大军）远抵那些地方，他们带回了黄金白银、女子妇人、驼峰高耸的骆驼与丰足的珍宝。",
"O my sworn and unsworn comrades, o my good companion! I departed!": "我那结盟与未结盟的同伴啊，我的良友啊！我去了！",
"O, my foal with a white forehead!": "我那白额的马驹啊！",
"On the second day, I killed their foot soldiers in great numbers.": "第二日，我大量杀伤他们的步卒。",
"One half of their army marched off in order to plunder our residences, the other half of their army came in order to fight.": "他们的军队一半开去劫掠我们的居所，另一半前来接战。",
"Or was there any lie in what I said?": "抑或我所说的话中有虚言？",
"Otuken, the capital of the First Turkic Khaganate and the Uyghur Khaganate.": "于都斤，突厥第一汗国与回鹘汗国的都城所在。",
"Our army horses were lean and army had no provisions": "我们的战马消瘦，军中没有粮秣。",
"Prince Kül put their army, which had come assaulting, to flight and we surrounded and killed a Tongra squad consisting of ten champion warriors at the funeral of Prince Tonga.": "阙特勤击溃了前来进攻的敌军；在同俄特勤的葬礼上，我们围歼了由十名勇士组成的同罗小队。",
"Rome, Byzantium, eastern Romans": "罗马、拜占庭、东罗马人。",
"Shad, a title, usually considered to be one step below the khagan": "设，官号，一般视为仅次于可汗一级。",
"Shandong (a region of China)": "山东（中国地区名）。",
"Since God gave them power, my father's, the kaghan's, army was like wolves, their enemies were like sheep.": "因上天赐其力量，我父可汗的军队如狼，其敌如羊。",
"Since their envoys, their good news and their blessings stopped coming to us, I went on a campaign in the summer.": "因他们的使者、佳音与祝祷不再传来，我于夏日出征。",
"Since they didn't send a caravan, I sent an army.": "因他们不遣商队前来，我便发兵。",
"Son of Heaven": "天子",
"Suffix creating a verb from a noun": "由名词构成动词的后缀。",
"Suffix forming first person plural imperative": "构成第一人称复数命令式的后缀。",
"Suffix forming first person singular imperative": "构成第一人称单数命令式的后缀。",
"Suffix forming nouns from verbs": "由动词构成名词的后缀。",
"Suffix forming second person plural imperative": "构成第二人称复数命令式的后缀。",
"Suffix forming second person singular imperative": "构成第二人称单数命令式的后缀。",
"Suffix forming third person imperative": "构成第三人称命令式的后缀。",
"Syr Darya": "锡尔河",
"Tangut people": "党项人",
"Taurus": "金牛座",
"Tengri, the chief deity of Turkic mythology.": "腾格里，突厥神话中的至上神。",
"That which is thin is easy to bend, they say; that which is tender is easy to break. If thin becomes thick, it is hard to bend it, they say; and if tender becomes tough, it is hard to break it, they say.": "据说，细者易折，嫩者易断；细者若变粗，便难以弯折；嫩者若变韧，便难以折断。",
"That year, during autumn, I marched forward […]": "那年秋天，我挥师前进……",
"The Elteber of Uyghurs fled towards and regrouped in the east, with around a hundred men.": "回鹘的俟利发率百余人东逃并重整队伍。",
"The Heaven above and the sacred Earth [below] approved the heavenly favor of my uncle, the khagan.": "上天与神圣的大地嘉许我叔父可汗所受的天佑。",
"The Heaven above and the sacred Earth [below] approved the heavenly favor of my uncle, the khagan.\n(literally, “ […] his heavenly favor [they] did not curse.”)": "上天与神圣的大地嘉许我叔父可汗所受的天佑。\n（直译：「……他们未曾诅咒他所受的天佑。」）",
"The Turkic lords (and) people worshipped (me), loved (me) and raised their eyes up.": "突厥的诸匐与百姓敬奉我、爱戴我，举目仰望。",
"The Turkic lords abondened their Turkic titles. Those lords who were in China held the Chinese titles and obeyed the Chinese emperor and gave their services to him for fifty years.": "突厥的首领们弃去了突厥的官号。身在汉地的那些首领受汉家官号、听命于唐帝，为其效力五十年。",
"The Turkic people's feet tottered and were about to be put to rout.": "突厥百姓步履踉跄，几近溃散。",
"The governor of the Uyghurs, together with about one hundred men, fled toward the east...": "回鹘的长官率百余人向东逃走……",
"The great irkin, ran away together with very few men.": "大俟斤仅率寥寥数人逃走。",
"The khagan of the Ten Tribes was our enemy.": "十姓部落的可汗是我们的敌人。",
"The people's throats were full.": "百姓的喉咙都是饱足的。",
"Their ministers, too, were presumably wise and tough.": "想必他们的大臣也是明智而强悍的。",
"Their officers, too, were presumably wise and tough.": "想必他们的将官也是明智而强悍的。",
"They brought scent[ed candle]s for the funeral and set them up for us. […]": "他们为葬礼送来香烛，并为我们设置妥当。……",
"They brought scented (candles) for the funeral and set them up for us.": "他们为葬礼送来香烛，并为我们设置妥当。",
"They brought their good saddle-horses, their black sables and blue squirrels in an uncountable number and left them all.": "他们带来良骑、黑貂与青鼠，数不胜数，尽数留下。",
"They gift us gold, silver and silk in abundance like so.": "他们如此这般以丰厚的金银与丝帛相赠。",
"They give us gold, silver and silk in abundance.": "他们以丰厚的金银与丝帛给予我们。",
"They hit (him) with more than a hundred arrows on his armor and caftan; (but he did not let the enemy hit him) even once on his face or head.": "他们在他的甲胄与外袍上射中百余箭，却未曾（让敌人）射中他的面部与头颅一次。",
"They made bow those, who had heads and made kneel those, who had knees.": "他们使有头者俯首，使有膝者屈膝。",
"Thirdly, he mounted Lord Yegen Silig's dressed bay horse and attacked.": "第三次，他骑上叶根·思力匐披挂整齐的赤褐马冲杀。",
"This many peoples cut out their hairs and tore their ears.": "这许多百姓割发裂耳（以志哀）。",
"Thus we stayed at the Altai Mountains.": "我们就这样驻留于阿尔泰山。",
"Tibet": "吐蕃",
"Tibet (a geographic region in Central Asia, the homeland of the Tibetan people)": "吐蕃（中亚地区名，藏人故土）。",
"To my thousand horses with no owners": "致我那千匹无主之马。",
"Tocharian people": "吐火罗人",
"Together with my younger brother, Prince Kül, and together with two shads, dying and getting lost, I won.": "我与我弟阙特勤、并两位设一同出战，虽死伤离散，终获胜利。",
"Tonyukuk, a tarkhan & adviser of the Second Turkic Khaganate": "暾欲谷，后突厥汗国达干、谋臣。",
"Tun Yegen Erkin.": "敦·叶根·俟斤。",
"Turk": "突厥人",
"Turkic people were famished.": "突厥百姓陷于饥馑。",
"Turkic people, the Göktürks": "突厥人、蓝突厥。",
"Turkic warlords lost their Turkic names and titles, [while] Chinese warlords kept their Chinese titles and served the Chinese emperor.": "突厥的将领失去了突厥的名号，而汉家将领仍保有汉家官号，为唐帝效力。",
"Used to form adverbs from adjectives": "由形容词构成副词。",
"Uyghurs": "回鹘人",
"We are few.": "我们人少。",
"We are going to stay.": "我们将留下。",
"We descended rolling.": "我们翻滚而下。",
"We finished his mausoleum, statues and paintings, and his inscription stone on the twenty-seventh day of the seventh month, on the Year of Monkey.": "猴年七月二十七日，我们完成了他的陵寝、石像、彩画与碑石。",
"We fought five times in a year.": "我们一年之内交战五次。",
"We fought with their kagan at the Songa mountains.": "我们在松阿山与他们的可汗交战。",
"We ordered (the army) to carry out a raid, while we left Prince Kül at home to command (the camp).": "我们下令（大军）出击劫掠，而留阙特勤在后统领营地。",
"We surrounded and killed a Tongra squad consisting of ten champion warriors at the funeral of Prince Tonga.": "在同俄特勤的葬礼上，我们围歼了由十名勇士组成的同罗小队。",
"We tied horses to the trees.": "我们把马系在树上。",
"We went on a campaign in the direction of six Sogdian states.": "我们朝六个粟特邦国的方向出征。",
"We went on campaigns up to the land of Kyrgyzes, beyond the Tannu-Ola mountains.": "我们出征直至唐努乌拉山以北的黠戛斯之地。",
"We were but a few [people], we were in bad shape.": "我们人数寥寥，处境窘迫。",
"Westwards I went on campaigns up to the Iron Gate beyond Syr Darya...": "我向西出征，直抵锡尔河以远的铁门关……",
"When I heard that there is only one road to the Sayan Mountains, and it is (now) closed (by snow), I said: 'If we go that way, it will not be good (for us)'.": "我听说通往萨彦岭只有一条路，而这条路（此时）已被大雪封闭，便说：「若走那条路，于我们不利。」",
"When I was seventeen years old, I went on a campaign against the Tangut.": "我十七岁那年出征党项。",
"When he fought seven times against the Nine Oghuzes, he poured them (on the river).": "他与九姓乌古斯交战七次，将他们（尽数）倾覆于河上。",
"When my father, the khagan, passed away, I was at the age of eight.": "我父可汗辞世时，我年方八岁。",
"When my oldest son died of being sick, I readily had Qu, the general, erect him a balbal.": "我的长子病故时，我即命曲将军为他竖立杀人石。",
"When there is valor, there is no sorrow, and when there is sorrow, then I am the hero Ezeru": "有勇则无忧；忧至之时，我便是英雄埃泽鲁。",
"When you are famished, you do not think of being full, [likewise,] you do not think of hunger once you get full [either.]": "你饥饿时不会想到饱足；同样，你饱足之后也不会想到饥饿。",
"While hunting...": "行猎之时……",
"Why should we feel overwhelmed because of being few?": "我们何须因人少而气沮？",
"Without having found their khan, the Turkic people were parted from the Chinese, and got themselves a khan.": "突厥百姓尚未寻得自己的可汗便与汉人分离，随后自立了一位可汗。",
"Yenisei Kyrgyz": "叶尼塞黠戛斯",
"You are stubborn.": "你很固执。",
"You will be wrong.": "你将有错。",
"You will die.": "你将死去。",
"[It is said that] they have created [it].": "据说是他们造的。",
"[The Chinese] do not let the people who know well and the people who are valiant tire themselves.": "（汉人）不让明智者与勇武者自劳其身。",
"[While] thinking that I shall feed [the people] […]": "我一面思量着要养活（百姓）……",
"[…] and served under them for fifty years.": "……并在他们麾下效力五十年。",
"[…] once you get full, you would not think of famishing again.": "……你一旦饱足，便不会再想到饥馑。",
"a Tibetan minister": "一位吐蕃大臣",
"a drink which is mixture of blood and koumiss that been used for taking an oath.": "血与马奶酒调和而成的饮品，用于盟誓。",
"a half": "一半",
"a kind of deer": "一种鹿",
"a kind of male deer; moose, elk, maral": "一种牡鹿；驼鹿、马鹿。",
